\section{Discussion}
The SPACE-TIME-REALITY Engine introduces a unified differential operator that merges geometry, dynamics, and verification. This structure enables computable curvature, autonomous event verification, multi-node dynamical interaction, stochastic perturbation modeling, and ledger-based causal history tracking. It suggests new directions for unified simulation architectures and autonomous verification systems.

\section{Conclusion}
We have defined a computational engine capable of evolving geometry, reality nodes, and verified events under a single governing equation. The SPACE-TIME-REALITY Engine provides a foundation for future work in multi-domain simulation and autonomous verification.

